00:16:28,334 --> 00:16:28,992
And it will do it.

207
00:16:29,134 --> 00:16:37,412
And it'll give you 10 little cards. And if you don't want to send something, you can always just press discard and it will discard it, and you can kind of just go through all of the emails.

208
00:16:37,632 --> 00:16:45,188
And so you ask it to send an email or a Slack message, then there's this little send gate where you approve, and then the message sends.

209
00:16:45,518 --> 00:16:47,076
And that's exactly how this works.

210
00:16:47,694 --> 00:16:54,112
And I think that this is gonna be one of the biggest trends with agents, especially with personal agents, in 2027.

211
00:16:54,318 --> 00:17:02,660
This is kind of something I've been demoing a lot for the past six months, and this is the UI that I've always wanted, where you can message the agent to do any task,

212
00:17:03,054 --> 00:17:08,592
and then it will respond with some text, and then it will show you the perfect interface for that task.

213
00:17:08,752 --> 00:17:16,832
In this case, it's Gmail and Slack, which is really useful, and then it shows you that interface, and then you take action within that mini

214
00:17:17,312 --> 00:17:23,152
For example, when you can like edit it, or you can respond to the app.

215
00:17:23,342 --> 00:17:25,828
It is like perfectly agent native.

216
00:17:26,126 --> 00:17:32,996
And then depending on what action you do in this mini app, it triggers an action, and then kind of the app gets updated.

217
00:17:33,232 --> 00:17:37,472
And I think it's like right now it's just email and Slack.

218
00:17:37,678 --> 00:17:40,032
Soon it's going to be basically everything.

219
00:17:40,238 --> 00:17:48,512
Okay, so now I want to talk about the final update of the day for Grokbot, which is routing traffic through your computer.

220
00:17:48,976 --> 00:17:57,456
If you go to GrokBot and you go down to settings and you go to computer and you scroll down to the bottom,

221
00:17:57,616 --> 00:18:05,252
you will see network and then route traffic through this computer. In my opinion, you should have this on.

222
00:18:05,550 --> 00:18:06,692
And I'll tell you why.

223
00:18:06,976 --> 00:18:15,616
This is because your bot has a computer in the cloud. If we go up to our bot right here, we can see that it actually runs on a computer.

224
00:18:15,982 --> 00:18:22,736
The reason why Grokbot and other personal agents are so powerful is they have access to a computer with a browser, right?

225
00:18:22,958 --> 00:18:24,416
It can navigate to

226
00:18:24,416 --> 00:18:29,476
target.com, for example, if you asked it to buy something on Target.

227
00:18:29,696 --> 00:18:38,052
However, the further you go down the path to buying something, Target's security will block bots from doing things,

228
00:18:38,416 --> 00:18:38,724
right?

229
00:18:39,086 --> 00:18:41,092
So like your bot has a cloud VM.

230
00:18:41,358 --> 00:18:43,812
And so VMs can get flagged as a bot.

231
00:18:44,016 --> 00:18:53,776
And this will actually prevent you from doing autonomous stuff, like buying from certain websites, filling out certain forms, or just doing a ton of tasks on the VM.

232
00:18:54,016 --> 00:18:59,856
And so routing through your computer makes it look like the bot is you. It uses your IP address.

233
00:19:00,046 --> 00:19:04,096
From Target's perspective, it will think that it is using your computer.

234
00:19:04,270 --> 00:19:12,736
And so routing the traffic through your computer makes it more likely the bots can actually do any task because it can route through your computer.

235
00:19:13,006 --> 00:19:17,296
And so this is a very simple thing to turn on, and I think it's incredibly useful.

236
